Third-party content and licensing
=================================

The MIT license in LICENSE covers the code. The data in this repository has
different terms, and this file exists to state them plainly.

data/corpus/*.md — CC BY-SA 3.0
-------------------------------
Built by src/ingest/ from Fandom wikis via the MediaWiki API. Fandom community
content is licensed CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported, so these corpus files are derivative
works under that license: attribution required, share-alike on redistribution.

Each passage carries its source in the heading, e.g.
    ## [series=frieren | page=Chapter_81 | section=Summary]
so every line traces back to the wiki page it came from. Source wikis are listed
by subdomain in data/series_registry.yaml (frieren.fandom.com,
kimetsu-no-yaiba.fandom.com, and so on).

data/scripts/*.md — derivative, CC BY-SA 3.0
--------------------------------------------
Authored prose, but grounded in and derived from the corpus above, and therefore
subject to the same share-alike terms. Their citations ([ch.81], [Doll Festival
Arc]) point back to corpus passages, which point back to Fandom.

Underlying works
----------------
The manga and anime summarised here are copyright their respective creators and
publishers. This project recounts plot as commentary and criticism. It generates
no character imagery: every [VISUAL:] cue is an atmospheric scene with
"no characters" in both the prompt and the negative prompt (see README).

Models
------
Piper (MIT) · Chatterbox (MIT, Resemble AI) · Stable Diffusion v1.5
(CreativeML Open RAIL-M — note its use-based restrictions) · faster-whisper
(MIT) · sentence-transformers (Apache 2.0). Model weights are not redistributed
here; each is fetched by its own tooling.

Scope
-----
This is a portfolio demonstration, not a publishing operation. Generating recaps
at scale, monetising them, or reproducing licensed art would raise questions this
repository does not attempt to answer.
